ubble telescope: 13.2 m (body length). Millennium Falcon: 34.75 m (overall length).\nHubble is about 13.2 m long; solar panels extend to either side of its body.\nThe Millennium Falcon is 34.75 m long in the official databank. Fictional; shown from above.","sources":["https://science.nasa.gov/mission/hubble/observatory/design/","https://www.starwars.com/databank/millennium-falcon"]},{"id":"size-v9-98","version":9,"kind":"scale","prompt":"How big is Humpback whale?","target":{"name":"Humpback whale","dimension":"upper adult length","shape":"sourced:humpback-whale"},"reference":{"name":"Gateway Arch","dimension":"height above ground","shape":"sourced:gateway-arch","measure":"192 m"},"bounds":[0.002,1.4],"answer":0.0953125,"explanation":"Humpback whale: 18.3 m (upper adult length). Gateway Arch: 192 m (height above ground).\nHumpbacks can reach about 60 ft (18.3 m).\nThe arch is about 192 m tall and approximately the same width from leg to leg.","sources":["https://www.fisheries.noaa.gov/species/humpback-whale","https://www.nps.gov/jeff/faqs.htm"]},{"id":"size-v9-99","version":9,"kind":"scale","prompt":"How big is AT-AT walker?","target":{"name":"AT-AT walker","dimension":"height","shape":"sourced:at-at"},"reference":{"name":"Saturn V","dimension":"height with Apollo spacecraft","shape":"sourced:saturn-v","measure":"110.6 m"},"bounds":[0.002,1.4],"answer":0.2034358047,"explanation":"AT-AT walker: 22.5 m (height). Saturn V: 110.6 m (height with Apollo spacecraft).\nThe original Imperial AT-AT stands 22.5 m tall. Fictional.\nNASA lists the complete Apollo–Saturn V at 363 ft (110.6 m).","sources":["https://www.starwars.com/databank/at-at-walker","https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/167718main_early_years.pdf"]}]'::jsonb);
